3. Calls upon all Member States to strengthen regional and international cooperation to prevent and suppress ISIL/Da’esh, its affiliates, and other terrorist groups designated by the Security Council, including through timely information-sharing, border security, law enforcement cooperation, countering terrorist financing, including by implementing Financial Action Task Force standards, enhancing information-sharing on terrorist financing networks, and addressing the risks posed by virtual assets and emerging technologies, and through capacity-building as appropriate, in full compliance with international law, including international human rights law, international refugee law and international humanitarian law, and encourages Member States to provide technical assistance and capacity-building, upon request, to States in the region, in particular developing countries, to strengthen border security, law enforcement cooperation and counter-terrorist financing;
