7. Calls for a comprehensive strategy for the al-Hol and Roj camps, including by accelerating the safe, dignified and voluntary repatriation, rehabilitation, reintegration and, where appropriate, prosecution of residents, with particular attention to children, and requests the Secretary-General to report on progress in this regard;
8. Urges all Member States to ensure accountability for crimes committed by ISIL/Da’esh and its affiliates, including terrorism, war crimes, crimes against humanity, and conflict-related sexual and gender-based violence, and all forms of violence against women and children, and to support the collection and preservation of evidence and the prosecution of perpetrators, including through support for the International, Impartial and Independent Mechanism for Syria and other relevant accountability mechanisms, and calls for survivor-centred and gender-responsive approaches, including access to justice, reparations and support services for victims of conflict-related sexual and gender-based violence;
